    "narrative": "For the May 7th slate, the Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable matchup against the Minnesota staff as **Brady House** and **Nasim Nunez** emerge as our top-tier plays. **Brady House** (63.81) benefits significantly from the matchup against Woods Richardson, whose 4.85 xERA combined with a favorable park factor allows **Brady House** to reach his ceiling. Similarly, **Nasim Nunez** (62.09) is a vital start today; while his batting order spot usually suppresses value, his elite speed profile\u2014a critical component for our 5x5 objectives\u2014coupled with the high-target SP skill rating makes him a mandatory inclusion. **Gunnar Henderson** (69.76) remains our anchor at the top of the order, and despite a moderate xERA from the opposing pitcher, his dynamic platoon advantage as a right-handed hitter against a righty arm keeps his efficiency score in the elite tier.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved **Coby Mayo**, who finished just shy of the 40.0 floor with a 38.03 efficiency score. While **Coby Mayo** offers significant power upside, he was excluded primarily due to a tough draw against Meyer and a bottom-third batting order position that limits his run production potential. We are proceeding cautiously with **Liam Hicks** (42.14); while he stays in the lineup to maintain depth, his negative platoon split against a lefty pitcher like Povich acts as a drag on his raw projections. We continue to monitor the status of **Luis Robert Jr.** on the IL, and with **Kyle Tucker** and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** sidelined by today\u2019s team off-days, our bench remains thin. We have successfully avoided the bottom-floor traps, but we will keep a close watch on weather reports to ensure no late-breaking winds dampen the park factors currently boosting **Josh Jung** (58.61) and his favorable wind-out conditions.",
